.TH HUGINN 1 "2026-11-16" "unheaded e6b73f22" "Unheaded Kingdom"
.SH NAME
huginn \- Huginn: report bare\-metal host metrics (CPU, memory, disks, network, processes) to the dashboard and VictoriaMetrics (ADR\-084).
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B huginn
[\fIOPTION\fR]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
Huginn: report bare\-metal host metrics (CPU, memory, disks, network, processes) to the dashboard and VictoriaMetrics (ADR\-084).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-cgroup\-root \fIDIR\fR
cgroup v2 DIR read for per\-cgroup series (cgroups.go, ADR\-147); empty turns them off (default /sys/fs/cgroup)
.TP
.B \-\-config \fISTRING\fR
path to YAML config file (optional) (default /etc/huginn.yaml)
.TP
.B \-\-host \fISTRING\fR
host label override (default: hostname or config)
.TP
.B \-\-interval \fIDURATION\fR
collection/push interval override
.TP
.B \-\-listen \fISTRING\fR
listen addresses override, comma\-separated (default 127.0.0.1:9110; huginn has no auth, so a wildcard is refused: name internal addresses)
.TP
.B \-\-pprof \fIADDR\fR
serve net/http/pprof on this loopback ADDR (e.g. 127.0.0.1:6060); off when empty
.TP
.B \-\-vm \fISTRING\fR
VictoriaMetrics URL override (empty string = no override)
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
display this help and exit
.TP
.B \-V, \-\-version
output version information and exit
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
huginn
huginn \-\-config /etc/huginn.yaml
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR unheaded (1)
